{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting Markdown to wiki renderer (pure capability)\n\n## Problem\nJira Data Center stores descriptions as lossy wiki markup. WikiTextCodec sends wiki strings without Markdown rendering, so raw Markdown appears literally. Whole-body pandoc conversion is unsafe for punctuation-dense prose, regular expressions, HTML-dense text, and ASCII tables. A corpus experiment measured that segmentation can enrich at least 0.68 of bodies and 0.78 of characters while preserving dangerous units.\n\nThis story adds only a pure renderer. It does not wire WikiTextCodec, OutboundFieldMapper, CREATE, or live send sites. disparaged-parodistic-shrew owns cutover, echo suppression, rollback, and second-pass convergence.\n\n## Existing contracts\n- WikiTextCodec.fit_outbound is not identity: it truncates strings above 32,767 characters and appends the established suffix. This stays unchanged.\n- normalize_outbound and to_wire remain identity on strings. decode_inbound remains identity on strings and maps None to an empty string.\n- The codec law normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t)) stays green.\n- rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py owns normalize_rich_text and stays unchanged.\n- ADR 0083 defines the vendor-adapter import boundary; jira_family must not import Cloud-specific adapters.\n\n## Dependency and optionality\nAdd optional extra jira-dc with exact pin pypandoc-binary==1.17. Core dependencies remain unchanged. Add its pypandoc probe and capability hint to src/rebar/_optional.py. Import it lazily at the renderer boundary with guard_import. Catch OptionalDependencyError and conversion failures, return the exact input, and emit one fallback warning per process. import rebar must not import pypandoc.\n\nAdd jira-dc to the dev self-reference so make install and Gerrit CI install the real wheel and bundled executable. Regenerate uv.lock. A non-skipping test imports pypandoc, proves the bundled executable exists, and performs real commonmark-to-jira conversion. A missing dependency or Jira writer therefore fails the gating suite instead of silently selecting fallback. A monkeypatched unit test separately covers fallback.\n\nTimeout/process hardening and GPL/SBOM work remain in ashy-waterlog-hamadryas.\n\n## Renderer\nAdd adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py:\n\n    render_markdown_to_wiki(markdown: str) -> str\n\nSplit input into ordered fenced-code blocks, headings, block quotes, blank-delimited paragraphs, and list items. Classification is deterministic and precedence ordered:\n\n1. Existing {noformat} and fenced-code blocks are protected complete units.\n2. ASCII tables are runs of at least two pipe-bearing lines whose delimiter row contains only pipes, colons, hyphens, and whitespace. Wrap the exact run once in {noformat}.\n3. Units containing an HTML start/end/self-closing tag pass through byte-identically.\n4. Units with a regex delimiter or metacharacter run outside inline-code spans pass through byte-identically.\n5. Remaining headings, quotes, list items, and prose paragraphs go to pandoc.\n\nPreserve existing {noformat} blocks byte-identically, so rendering never nests them. Preserve block order and blank-line separation.\n\nReplace prose arrows (->, <-, <->, =>) with Unicode before pandoc. A scanner excludes fenced code and backtick-delimited inline spans, so obj->method() stays exact.\n\nRender safe units with pypandoc using input commonmark, output jira, and --wrap=none. Measured checklist input \"- [ ] todo\" yields exact Jira output \"* \\\\[ ] todo\"; tests assert this instead of assuming native task-list markup. A fenced python block yields {code:python}...{code}. A heading yields the measured h1 anchor form.\n\n## Hermetic corpus\nCommit sanitized JSON fixtures under tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/. They are never fetched. They include 179 code-arrow bodies and 70 table-erosion bodies, including the 9115-to-9110 ratchet example. Every fixture declares protected excerpts and safe renderable excerpts, so unchanged fallback cannot satisfy the oracle.\n\n## Testing\nHappy path uses real pypandoc: a heading, checklist, and fenced code become the measured h1 anchor form, \"* \\\\[ ] todo\", and {code:python} in original order.\n\nHeld-out tests prove:\n- A mixed body wraps an ASCII table once, converts a prose arrow, preserves an inline-code arrow, and leaves regex/HTML-dense blocks exact.\n- Existing {noformat} stays exact through repeated rendering.\n- All 179 arrow fixtures retain each declared protected excerpt and convert each declared safe excerpt.\n- All 70 erosion fixtures retain exact table bytes through five passes.\n- Missing import and conversion exceptions return exact input with one warning per process.\n- Every enrichment-eligible fixture has a safe unit whose output differs. Tests compute exact rendered-body and rendered-character ratios, then assert body ratio >= 0.68 and character ratio >= 0.78. They compare all protected excerpts byte-for-byte and reject loss, duplication, or reordering.\n\nExisting WikiTextCodec truncation, identity, and codec-law tests stay unmodified. No contention test applies: this is a pure transformation plus process boundary, without store operations, retry/backoff, or cached store state.\n\n## Verification\nCollect and execute the new unit nodes without skips, then run the same repository gates used by CI: env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint, env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck, and env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test. The real-pandoc test hard-fails when the dependency or Jira writer is absent.\n\n## Surface parity census\n- CLI: out of scope; no command exposes this capability.\n- MCP/API: out of scope; no tool exposes it.\n- Library facade: out of scope; no public import is added.\n- Automated callers: out of scope; disparaged-parodistic-shrew owns caller wiring and E2E coverage.\n- Dual direction: out of scope; this is one-way and cutover owns convergence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Safe units render through real pypandoc in original order; checked by the non-skipping happy-path unit test.\n- [ ] Regex-heavy units pass through byte-identically; checked by the mixed-body held-out test.\n- [ ] HTML-dense units pass through byte-identically; checked by the mixed-body held-out test.\n- [ ] Prose arrows convert before pandoc; checked by the mixed-body held-out test.\n- [ ] Fenced-code arrows stay exact; checked across all 179 arrow fixtures.\n- [ ] Inline-code arrows stay exact; checked across all 179 arrow fixtures.\n- [ ] Detected ASCII tables receive exactly one {noformat} wrapper; checked by repeated-render tests.\n- [ ] Existing {noformat} blocks never nest; checked by five renderer passes.\n- [ ] All 70 erosion fixtures preserve declared table bytes; checked by five renderer passes including the ratchet body.\n- [ ] jira-dc pins pypandoc-binary==1.17; checked from the locked dev/CI install.\n- [ ] Real pandoc Jira rendering is available; checked by a non-skipping conversion test under `make test`.\n- [ ] Missing pypandoc returns exact input; checked by the fallback unit test.\n- [ ] Conversion failure returns exact input; checked by the fallback unit test.\n- [ ] Fallback warning emits once per process; checked by repeated fallback calls.\n- [ ] Corpus rendered-body ratio is >= 0.68; checked from the exact computed ratio.\\n- [ ] Corpus rendered-character ratio is >= 0.78; checked from the exact computed ratio.\n- [ ] Declared protected excerpts have zero corruption; checked byte-for-byte.\n- [ ] Existing WikiTextCodec contracts remain green under `make test`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786569375253628001,"uuid":"8b6b5034-9a68-47c4-8166-f5a3c2700378"}